// The prologue's ship deck "Fehler" (docs/STORY.md, Prolog im Detail): one plane, 1 m a character, x east, y north.
// The first row of the grid is the north edge (y = 179), the last the south edge (y = 0); a character at column x of
// the row for y covers [x, x+1] x [y, y+1]. Read by import/Machines.Import/Planets/DeckParser.cs and tools/deck/deck.mjs.
// Legend: # wall (8 m)   . floor   v duct (crawl only)   ^ duct lip (raised mouth, crawl only)   g grate wall (blocks
// movement, shots and sight pass)   c high cover, 2 m (crates, consoles)   = catwalk (visual height only)
// A-Z a door or gate slot named in DOORS (an artefact while closed).
// Sections: DOORS letter name kind state | MARKERS name x y angle [tags] | PROPS name type x y angle id |
// ZONES name x0 y0 x1 y1 [tags] | LIGHTS name zone on|off|emergency | CAMS name x y z yaw pitch | RAILS name x y z ...
// Angles in degrees, 0 east, 90 north. Room titles:
//   R2    Bucht 6 (Ike)
//   R1    Bucht 7 (L-7)
//   R3    Bucht 8 (Bob)
//   R0    Buchtengang
//   R4    Wartungsdeck A
//   WL    West link
//   EL    East link
//   R5    Lager
//   R7    Schaltraum
//   S     Service passage
//   R6    Wartungsdeck B
//   R8    Vorraum Rechnerkern
//   R9    Rechnerkern
//   R10   Hauptgang
//   R10a  Kaserne-Lift
//   P1    Parallelgang 1
//   P1s   Parallelgang 1, stub to the spine
//   P2    Parallelgang 2
//   K     Kabelgang
//   R12   Kreuzung
//   R13   Werkstatt
//   R13a  Werkstattgang
//   R14   Reparaturnische
//   R15   Notgang
//   R15a  Notgang, mouth into the pod bay
//   R16   Pod-Bucht

DECK prolog 270 180
GRID
